Make closure an evolving physical and working design throughout the mine life (@mine-closure-planning: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN", #source "../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ", #source "../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Rehabilitation-soils-vegetation-erosion-and-completion-evidence.lingua#r_1TQVJSAJR18YCGPRA48JZXJ6XQ") { r_5JNBRXVEJ85P5ZK044HDSF2KRC
**Read:** [Mine closure — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN), the complete handbook and its full planning/implementation cases; [Mine rehabilitation — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ), complete outcome, material, and monitoring discussions; [Water stewardship — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM), the complete long-term water-management context.

Closure changes landforms, openings, water systems, structures, contamination pathways, use, livelihoods, and responsibilities. It is planned from exploration/design and revised with what operation reveals. A financial allowance or a statement that a site will be restored does not define a physical outcome or demonstrate its persistence.

Describe the intended future uses and conditions with the people affected, the baseline and uncertainties, the material/structure inventory, and the remaining hazards and obligations. Compare progressive rehabilitation, final works, temporary shutdown, and premature closure. Different schedules and incomplete extraction can leave different accessible materials and water/ground conditions.

Build quantities, work sequences, dependencies, resources, uncertainty, verification observations, and the basis of long-term provision. Explain which performance criteria test an outcome and which only record that an activity occurred. Completion, transfer, or relinquishment requires its actual technical and jurisdictional evidence, not a general handbook declaration.

**Work:** reconstruct the complete closure basis for a published mine case. Compare the original assumptions with subsequent observations and identify the resulting design changes. Produce a material/water/landform account and a feasible work sequence for normal and early closure. Defend measurable performance criteria, monitoring duration/interpretation, and who will preserve knowledge, respond to failure, and maintain unresolved systems.

**Continue:** [Evaluate rehabilitation through soil, water, ecology, material behavior, and observed outcomes](Rehabilitation-soils-vegetation-erosion-and-completion-evidence.lingua#r_1TQVJSAJR18YCGPRA48JZXJ6XQ).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
